Third-party work this repository builds on:

Mahi-Mahi
  The DAG ordering layer in crates/consensus/src/mahi follows the committer
  organization of the Mahi-Mahi reference implementation by Pasindu Tennage
  and contributors (https://github.com/PasinduTennage/mahi-mahi-consensus,
  revision 13a2819800ad3b192ab3c54dfe3ec4d0b34ae361), and the protocol of:
  Jovanovic, Kokoris Kogias, Kumara, Sonnino, Tennage, and Zablotchi.
  "Mahi-Mahi: Low-Latency Asynchronous BFT DAG-Based Consensus." ICDCS 2025.

Mysticeti
  The Mahi-Mahi reference implementation builds on Mysticeti by Mysten Labs
  (https://github.com/MystenLabs/mysticeti), licensed under the Apache
  License, Version 2.0. The selectable Mysticeti-named commit rule in this
  repository follows:
  Babel, Chursin, Danezis, Kichidis, Kokoris-Kogias, Koshy, Sonnino, and Tian.
  "Mysticeti: Reaching the Latency Limits with Uncertified DAGs." NDSS 2025.

This repository's configuration differs from both protocols (round-robin
leaders, one leader slot, no pipeline, no shared coin). Their published
safety and liveness results do not transfer to it.

Other third-party Rust crates are listed in Cargo.lock and remain under their
own licences.
